# Python bytecode from the host-side K1 tools.
tools/__pycache__/

# Locally generated Realtek firmware payloads.  The vendor package installed on
# this board states no redistribution license for its firmware binaries, so the
# extracted arrays stay out of the contest repository.  Regenerate them with
# tools/extract_rtl8852bs_bt_patch.py (Bluetooth patch/config) when
# CONFIG_K1_BT_H5_VENDOR_FIRMWARE is enabled.  The Wi-Fi NICCE image kept in
# chip/k1/k1_rtl8852bs_u2_nicce_fw.inc is deliberately NOT ignored: it is part
# of the GPL-2.0-only component and docs/K1_SOURCE_AND_LICENSES.md records its
# provenance, length and SHA-256.
chip/k1/k1_rtl8852bs_bt_patch.inc
chip/k1/k1_rtl8852bs_u2_nic_fw.inc
